  "source_scope_and_parameters": {
    "objects": "Actual p_eta(y)=argmin_x[V(x)+||x-y||²/(2eta)]; standardGaussian G~N(0,I); H_y(G)=ghat_eta(y;G)=gradV(p_eta(y)+sqrteta G). Source g_eta=gradV_eta where exp(-V_eta)=exp(-V)*N(0,eta I). Decomposition H_y=g_eta(y)+b_eta(y)+xi_eta(y;G), E_gamma xi_eta=0. Gamma/output law differs from true posterior R_eta,y and affine standardized r_y.",
    "domains": "Source finite Euclidean R^d, ordinary Euclidean inner product/norm, standard centered covariance-identity Gaussian probability. Source all y,u,yprime,G,Gprime in R^d. Possible coordinate-free finite-Hilbert/Borel,0D,or measurable parameter-family versions are future explicit representation elaborations, not primary printed hypotheses.",
    "quantifiers": "Every eta>0 inherited Section3.1; fixed eta, every y and every vector u. Literal (4.3) absorbs both signs by arbitrary u: for any direction a and signed real t set u=t a, including t=0/a=0. One actual expectation/center for a fixed y precedes all t; future domain theorem must construct these expectations from actual law, not take them as certificates.",
    "assumptions": "V genuine C2 globally; standing0<alpha<=beta, normalizedbeta1 and alpha=kappa^-1 withkappa>=1; pointwise kappa^-1 I<=HessV<=I. Eta>0 with no analytic eta upper bound for Lemma4.2. Source numerical-prox call eta<=1/(2beta) and adjacentLemma4.1 eta<=1 are separate. Actual measurability/Lipschitz/firstmoments/exponentialintegrability/proxexistence are dependencies or outputs, not extra public source assumptions.",
    "conclusion": "Printed (4.3): E_gamma exp(<u,xi_eta(y;G)>)<=exp(eta||u||²/2). Proposed bounded prerequisite only: actual scalar h_a(z)=<a,H_y(z)> has genuine first moment m_a=int h_a dgamma, and exp(t(h_a-m_a)) is integrable for every real signed t. No sharp inequality established or approved by this preread.",
    "scopes": "A necessary actual exponential-domain/centering prerequisite for eventual source(4.3); domain-only output is strictly less than sharp centered MGF. No candidate/signature/API/code/proof review, no SAU/VERIFIED. Bias4.2, FIRST4.6 W2/Talagrand/LSI,fullLemma4.2,posteriorjointMarkovfamily,algorithms/main/work/composition remain outside.",
    "constant_dependencies": "Literal exponenteta||u||²/2; for u=t a becomes eta t²||a||²/2. Actual h_a Lipschitz coefficientsqrteta||a|| under normalizedbeta1. No d in sharp MGF constant; a dimension-dependent radial exponential envelope could establish only finiteness, not sharpdimensionfree concentration."
  },
